# Capitalization

Never use all caps (`UPPERCASE`, `uppercase` CSS, or `toUpperCase()` for UI copy).

Default to **sentence case** for anything that needs capitalization:

- Nav labels: `Foundations`, not `FOUNDATIONS`
- Headings, buttons, badges, tabs, section labels
- Mono / code samples in docs: show tokens as written (`--brand-primary`), not forced uppercase

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<p className="uppercase">Foundations</p>
<span className="font-mono uppercase">VAR(--BRAND-PRIMARY)</span>

// ✅ GOOD
<p>Foundations</p>
<span className="font-mono">var(--brand-primary)</span>
```

Title Case is only for proper nouns or established product names (e.g. `Standard UI`). Prefer sentence case for UI chrome and docs headings when in doubt.
